{
  "note": "Digests of inputs, rayHue, mateSeenAt and coverTotals (and the gathered row counts) after every tick. First recorded from the JS ray march before T11 deleted it; re-recorded from the kernel after the keepers merge (#328) and the eat-choice switch changed the default world, the kernel having matched the goldens #328 pinned with the JS ray march (docs/designs/wasm-kernels.md); test/sim/helpers/sense-reference.js The stepped digests were re-recorded from the kernels at body-genes T7: the pooled-v6 layout changes what a random brain does, so every stepped world moves; the fuzz digests do not depend on the layout and are unchanged. Re-recorded again at body-genes T31, when pooling started reading the body sense lanes and every stepped world moved. Stepped digests re-recorded from the Rust kernels when a startled herd stopped holding its centroid (role-budget T21a, `summarizeGroup`): the herds move differently in every busy world, and the cases that moved are named in docs/notes/2026-11.md. Stepped digests re-recorded for smoke dropped toward a hunter in front (feat(sim)!: smokeAimArc): a world where a releaser has a hunter ahead drops its cloud elsewhere.",
